The `DeciderSpecification` pattern (given/when/then testing for deciders) and
the `Decider` type structure are adapted from Emmett's `deciderSpecification.ts`
and related modules. The DCB adaptation replaces stream-based concurrency with
tag/boundary-based `AppendCondition` assertions and adds `.thenCondition()` for
consistency boundary testing.

The consumer/processor pattern (session-scoped processor lock, CAS-versioned
checkpoints, start-position policies, consumer lifecycle) is adapted from
Emmett's `postgreSQLProcessor.ts`, `processorsLocks.ts`,
`storeProcessorCheckpoint.ts`, and `processorStartPositions.ts`. The DCB
adaptation uses plain `sequence_position` checkpoints (no composite
transaction_id/global_position), a distinct `P:` advisory lock namespace, and
tag/boundary-based event queries.
